  "critique": {
    "axis": "accessibility",
    "evidence": "Mandate passes measured keyboard traversal and visible-focus checks at all viewports, reports no touch-target violations or viewport overflow, and shows no changed elements under reduced motion. However, WCAG contrast remains unproven: serious color-contrast checks are incomplete for the diagram labels at every viewport and for multiple tablet/mobile header items. The responsive header also keeps 13–14 links in the tab order while many are visually clipped behind the compact navigation.",
    "fix": "Provide measured contrast ratios for every unresolved diagram and header label, using solid computable backgrounds or higher-contrast colors as needed. At tablet/mobile widths, remove clipped navigation links from the active tab order when collapsed, expose them through an accessible “More” control, and verify focus visibility after opening it.",
